<title>GERMANY: German Q1 retail sales down real 1.0 pct.</title>
<headline>German Q1 retail sales down real 1.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> GERMAN RETAIL SALES	     Q1 96</p>
<p> Yr/yr pct change (real)	 -1.0</p>
<p> Yr/yr pct change (nominal)    -0.2</p>
<p>NOTE - The statistics office said that a new 1996 series of retail sales data, based on a wider representative sample of 20,000 businesses, would replace figures published earlier based on a narrower survey group.  </p>
<p>NOTE - First quarter retail sales data are preliminary. Data do not include vehicle and petrol sales. The statistics office had said that retail sales fell in March by a real three percent. Figures are not seasonally or calendar adjusted.</p>
<p>-- Douglas Busvine, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150  </p>
